.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt NQDINFER 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqdinfer ,
.Nm nqdschk
.Nd infer and check the schema of a CSV file
.Sh LIBRARY
libnqd, \-lnqd \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In nqd.h
.Bd -literal
typedef struct {
  char delim;   /* 0 for ',' */
  int noheader; /* the first line is data */
  int ranges;   /* pin number and date ranges */
} nqdcsvopt;
.Ed
.Ft int
.Fo nqdinfer
.Fa "const char *dir" "const char *path" "const nqdcsvopt *o"
.Fa "char *out" "size_t cap" "size_t *outlen" "char *why" "size_t wcap"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo nqdschk
.Fa "const char *dir" "const char *schema" "size_t n" "nqdrep **rep"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn nqdinfer
reads the CSV file
.Fa path
(relative to
.Fa dir )
and writes its schema to
.Fa out ,
a
.Ql schemas
element
.Pq Xr noqtis-data 5
in canonical JSON, to give to
.Xr nqdput 3 :
column names (from the header, or V1, V2, ... with
.Fa noheader ) ,
the narrowest type of each, whether it has missing values (the empty
field and
.Ql NA ) ,
the row count pinned, and with
.Fa ranges
each number or date column's range.
.Xr noqtis-schema 1
says what each type accepts.
.Fa o
may be
.Dv NULL
for the defaults.
On failure a sentence goes to
.Fa why .
.Pp
.Fn nqdschk
checks the file named by the
.Ql schemas
element
.Fa schema
.Pf ( Fa n
bytes of JSON) against it and reports one
.Ql schema
row per problem (the first ten, then a count) or one passing row, and
one
.Ql rule
row per rule, as
.Xr nqdchk 3
does for every schema of a record.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn nqdinfer :
.Dv NQOK ;
.Dv NQEBUF
with
.Fa *outlen
set when
.Fa cap
is too small;
.Dv NQEDEC
for a file that is not CSV, rows of different lengths or a column name
twice;
.Dv NQELIM
over the reader's limits (a field 1 MiB, a line 16 MiB or 16,384
fields);
.Dv NQEIO
for a file that cannot be read;
.Dv NQEARG
for a bad path or delimiter.
.Pp
.Fn nqdschk :
.Dv NQOK
when every row passed,
.Dv NQEVRFY
otherwise (an element that is not a schema is a failed row), with
.Fa *rep
set; free it with
.Xr nqdrepfree 3 .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-schema 1 ,
.Xr nqdchk 3 ,
.Xr nqdnew 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-data 5
.Sh STANDARDS
.Rs
.%R RFC 4180
.%T Common Format and MIME Type for Comma-Separated Values (CSV) Files
.Re
